  {
    "episode_id": 82221,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/2/82221.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 16,
    "turn_text": "Consider this. An Alabama court says a person can be held legally responsible if frozen embryos are destroyed, and this could go beyond Alabama to other states that have personhood statutes saying life and rights begin at conception. From NPR, I'm Ari Shapiro. It's Tuesday, February 27th.",
